ormation about the `data` and `target` object.\n806 | \n807 |         .. versionadded:: 0.18\n808 | \n809 |     as_frame : bool, default=False\n810 |         If True, the data is a pandas DataFrame including columns with\n811 |         appropriate dtypes (numeric). The target is\n812 |         a pandas DataFrame or Series depending on the number of target columns.\n813 |         If `return_X_y` is True, then (`data`, `target`) will be pandas\n814 |         DataFrames or Series as described below.\n815 | \n816 |         .. versionadded:: 0.23\n817 | \n818 |     Returns\n819 |     -------\n820 |     data : :class:`~sklearn.utils.Bunch`\n821 |         Dictionary-like object, with the following attributes.\n822 | \n823 |         data : {ndarray, dataframe} of shape (1797, 64)\n824 |             The flattened data matrix. If `as_frame=True`, `data` will be\n825 |             a pandas DataFrame.\n826 |         target: {ndarray, Series} of shape (1797,)\n827 |             The classification target. If `as_frame=True`, `target` will be\n828 |             a pandas Series.\n829 |         feature_names: list\n830 |             The names of the dataset columns.\n831 |         target_names: list\n832 |             The names of target classes.\n833 | \n834 |             .. versionadded:: 0.20\n835 | \n836 |         frame: DataFrame of shape (1797, 65)\n837 |             Only present when `as_frame=True`. DataFrame with `data` and\n838 |             `target`.\n839 | \n840 |             .. versionadded:: 0.23\n841 |         images: {ndarray} of shape (1797, 8, 8)\n842 |             The raw image data.\n843 |         DESCR: str\n844 |             The full description of the dataset.\n845 | \n846 |     (data, target) : tuple if ``return_X_y`` is True\n847 | \n848 |         .. versionadded:: 0.18\n849 | \n850 |     This is a copy of the test set of the UCI ML hand-written digits datasets\n851 |     https://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/datasets/Optical+Recognition+of+Handwritten+Digits\n852 | \n853 |     Examples\n854 |     --------\n855 |     To load the data and visualize the images::\n856 | \n857 |         >>> from sklearn.datasets import load_digits\n858 |         >>> digits = load_digits()\n859 |         >>> print(digits.data.shape)\n860 |         (1797, 64)\n861 |         >>> import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n862 |         >>> plt.gray()\n863 |         >>> plt.matshow(digits.images[0])\n864 |         <...>\n865 |         >>> plt.show()\n866 |     \"\"\"\n867 | \n868 |     data, fdescr = load_gzip_compressed_csv_data(\n869 |         data_file_name=\"digits.csv.gz\", descr_file_name=\"digits.rst\", delimiter=\",\"\n870 |     )\n871 | \n872 |     target = data[:, -1].astype(int, copy=False)\n873 |     flat_data = data[:, :-1]\n874 |     images = flat_data.view()\n875 |     images.shape = (-1, 8, 8)\n876 | \n877 |     if n_class < 10:\n878 |         idx = target < n_class\n879 |         flat_data, target = flat_data[idx], target[idx]\n880 |         images = images[idx]\n881 | \n882 |     feature_names = [\n883 |         \"pixel_{}_{}\".format(row_idx, col_idx)\n884 |         for row_idx in range(8)\n885 |         for col_idx in range(8)\n886 |     ]\n887 | \n888 |     frame = None\n889 |     target_columns = [\n890 |         \"target\",\n891 |     ]\n892 |     if as_frame:\n893 |         frame, flat_data, target = _convert_data_dataframe(\n894 |             \"load_digits\", flat_data, target, feature_names, target_columns\n895 |         )\n896 | \n897 |     if return_X_y:\n898 |         return flat_data, target\n899 | \n900 |     return Bunch(\n901 |         data=flat_data,\n902 |         target=target,\n903 |         frame=frame,\n904 |         feature_names=feature_names,\n905 |         target_names=np.arange(10),\n906 |         images=images,\n907 |         DESCR=fdescr,\n908 |     )\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/datasets/_base.py:load_linnerud`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1008 | def load_linnerud(*, return_X_y=False, as_frame=False):\n1009 |     \"\"\"Load and return the physical excercise linnerud dataset.\n1010 | \n1011 |     This dataset is suitable for multi-ouput regression tasks.\n1012 | \n1013 |     ==============   ============================\n1014 |     Samples total    20\n1015 |     Dimensionality   3 (for both data and target)\n1016 |     Features         integer\n1017 |     Targets          integer\n1018 |     ==============   ============================\n1019 | \n1020 |     Read more in the :ref:`User Guide <linnerrud_dataset>`.\n1021 | \n1022 |     Parameters\n1023 |     ----------\n1024 |     return_X_y : bool, default=False\n1025 |         If True, returns ``(data, target)`` instead of a Bunch object.\n1026 |         See below for more information about the `data` and `target` object.\n1027 | \n1028 |         .. versionadded:: 0.18\n1029 | \n1030 |     as_frame : bool, default=False\n1031 |         If True, the data is a pandas DataFrame including columns with\n1032 |         appropriate dtypes (numeric, string or categorical). The target is\n1033 |         a pandas DataFrame or Series depending on the number of target columns.\n1034 |         If `return_X_y` is True, then (`data`, `target`) will be pandas\n1035 |         DataFrames or Series as described below.\n1036 | \n1037 |         .. versionadded:: 0.23\n1038 | \n1039 |     Returns\n1040 |     -------\n1041 |     data : :class:`~sklearn.utils.Bunch`\n1042 |         Dictionary-like object, with the following attributes.\n1043 | \n1044 |         data : {ndarray, dataframe} of shape (20, 3)\n1045 |             The data matrix. If `as_frame=True`, `data` will be a pandas\n1046 |             DataFrame.\n1047 |         target: {ndarray, dataframe} of shape (20, 3)\n1048 |             The regression targets. If `as_frame=True`, `target` will be\n1049 |             a pandas DataFrame.\n1050 |         feature_names: list\n1051 |             The names of the dataset columns.\n1052 |         target_names: list\n1053 |             The names of the target columns.\n1054 |         frame: DataFrame of shape (20, 6)\n1055 |             Only present when `as_frame=True`. DataFrame with `data` and\n1056 |             `target`.\n1057 | \n1058 |             .. versionadded:: 0.23\n1059 |         DESCR: str\n1060 |             The full description of the dataset.\n1061 |         data_filename: str\n1062 |             The path to the location of the data.\n1063 |         target_filename: str\n1064 |             The path to the location of the target.\n1065 | \n1066 |             .. versionadded:: 0.20\n1067 | \n1068 |     (data, target) : tuple if ``return_X_y`` is True\n1069 | \n1070 |         .. versionadded:: 0.18\n1071 |     \"\"\"\n1072 |     data_filename = \"linnerud_exercise.csv\"\n1073 |     target_filename = \"linnerud_physiological.csv\"\n1074 | \n1075 |     # Read header and data\n1076 |     with resources.open_text(DATA_MODULE, data_filename) as f:\n1077 |         header_exercise = f.readline().split()\n1078 |         f.seek(0)  # reset file obj\n1079 |         data_exercise = np.loadtxt(f, skiprows=1)\n1080 | \n1081 |     with resources.open_text(DATA_MODULE, target_filename) as f:\n1082 |         header_physiological = f.readline().split()\n1083 |         f.seek(0)  # reset file obj\n1084 |         data_physiological = np.loadtxt(f, skiprows=1)\n1085 | \n1086 |     fdescr = load_descr(\"linnerud.rst\")\n1087 | \n1088 |     frame = None\n1089 |     if as_frame:\n1090 |         (frame, data_exercise, data_physiological) = _convert_data_dataframe(\n1091 |             \"load_linnerud\",\n1092 |             data_exercise,\n1093 |             data_physiological,\n1094 |             header_exercise,\n1095 |             header_physiological,\n1096 |         )\n1097 |     if return_X_y:\n1098 |         return data_exercise, data_physiological\n1099 | \n1100 |     return Bunch(\n1101 |         data=data_exercise,\n1102 |         feature_names=header_exercise,\n1103 |   